sV8.3 We collect Personal Information which you provide us voluntarily
p12
I1
sVIf you are using Google Android device with Android 2.3 or a later version, you can find the ad identifier settings in the app drawer under Google Settings>
p13
I1
sVHugs N Hearts and Third Parties do not know the identity of the User from whom Non-personal Information has been collected.
p14
I1
sVPersonal Information is collected in order to:
p15
I1
sVWe collect Information which the User voluntary provides Hugs N Hearts through the Apps for Everyone \u201cAsk a Question\u201d type of feature, when he/she opens an Account or when he/she makes his/her User Generated Content available to others.
p16
I1
sVPurpose of the collection: The information abovementioned is collected and processed solely for the purpose of supporting Hugs N Hearts\u2019 internal operations.
p17
I1
sVIt is hereby clarified that no street name or city/town name is collected.
p18
I1
sVFor avoidance of doubt, Hugs N Hearts may transfer and disclose Non-personal Information to third parties at its discretion.
p19
I1
sVWe may share Personal Information only in the following cases:
p20
I1
sVThe abovementioned Kids Non-personal Information and Kids\u2019 Persistent Device Identifier are collected either by Hugs N Hearts or by Third Parties through the Users\u2019 use of the Kids Apps, including, without limitation, through Third Parties\u2019 SDK embedded in our Kids Apps.
p21
I1
sVIn addition, we collect Personal information which you voluntarily provide when you use the "Log in with Facebook" feature (as further detailed above).
p22
I1
sVYou hereby agree that we may use the contact details you provided us to inform you regarding competitions we may hold, our new products and/or services, and to send to you other material.
p23
I1
sVBy using the Social Features and/or the Game Center Features you hereby agree and understand that the applicable Social Networks or Platforms may collect certain Personal Information, such as your IP address, Non-personal Information and may set cookies and/or other web tracking technologies to enable the functionality of the Social Features and/or the Game Center Features.
p24
I1
sVYou understand that where you allow interaction with any third party Social Network or Platform, we may share data about you with your contacts (and vice versa) in order that you may enjoy social elements.
p25
I1
sVIf Third Parties whose SDK is installed in the Kids Apps collect Kids Non-personal Information, Kids\u2019 Persistent Device Identifier and/or any other information directly from Kids, such collection and processing is governed by such Third Parties\u2019 privacy policies and not by this Privacy Policy.
p26
I1
sVPlease note that some of the Apps for Everyone include a sharing feature which allows Users to share their User Generated Content with others.
p27
I1
sVPlease note that we may transfer such information to a country and jurisdiction that does not have the same data protection laws as your jurisdiction, and you consent to such transfer of information.
p28
I1
sg3
I1
sVFor avoidance of doubt, Hugs N Hearts may transfer and disclose Kids Non-personal Information to third parties at its discretion.
p29
I1
sVIf the User uses the "Log in with Facebook" feature, then such User agrees that we may share his/her name and/or profile picture and/or his/her game data (such as moves, progress in our games and scores) with respect to the applicable Apps for Everyone, with Users who have also used the "Log in with Facebook" feature in connection with the applicable App for Everyone or with the User's Facebook contacts.
p30
I1
sVThe Vendors may collect Personal Information from Users who wish to purchase Merchandise, which is required in order to enable the purchase transaction (for example, the User's address in order to deliver him/her the Merchandise, the User's payment information in order to enable the billing and the processing of payment via various payment methods, etc.).
p31
I1
sVThis information will be collected, maintained, shared, transferred and/or used in accordance with the applicable Vendors privacy policy and terms of use.
p32
I1
sg4
I3
sVYou hereby understand and agree that when you share content via Social Networks or Platforms that your content may become public and any person may re-post-it.
p33
I1
sVAdditionally, if a User uses the "Log in with Facebook" feature (which functionality is described in the TOU) then Facebook provides us with access to (i) certain information about such User as is stored in the User\u2019s Facebook account, namely, the User's public profile (i.e., User's name, profile picture, email address, gender and other public information) and his/her list of friends and/or any other information which is detailed and displayed to the User in the notice which appears during the "Log in with Facebook" process.
p34
I1
